{"name":"Golden Lotus","hex":"#e9dbc4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"lotus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the genus Nelumbo of aquatic plants in the family Nelumbonaceae.","A water lily (Nymphaea), especially those of Egypt or India. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lotus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Musella lasiocarpa","blocks":[{"text":"Musella lasiocarpa, commonly known as Chinese dwarf banana, golden lotus banana or Chinese yellow banana, is the sole species in the genus Musella. It is thus a close relative of bananas, and also a member of the family Musaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Musella_lasiocarpa2.jpg/330px-Musella_lasiocarpa2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musella_lasiocarpa","wikidata":"Q5100760"},{"title":"Golden Lotus (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Lotus is an album by pianist Kenny Barron, recorded in 1980 and first released on the Muse label in 1982 before being reissued on CD by 32 Records with Sunset to Dawn in 1997."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/94/Golden_Lotus_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Lotus_(album)","wikidata":"Q28453416"},{"title":"Golden Lotus (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Lotus is a musical written and composed by George Chiang. The musical is based on the classic 17th-century Chinese novel Jin Ping Mei. Set amidst the dying, war-torn years of Song dynasty China, the musical tells the story of the Golden Lotus, whose desire for true love leads her into a web of deception and desperation with the valiant tiger slayer Wu Sung, the rich and powerful Xi Men, and the humble peddler Wu Da."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/43/Golden_Lotus_%282021%29_Musical_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Lotus_(musical)","wikidata":"Q55612775"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Musella_lasiocarpa_at_Hampton_Court_Flower_Show.jpg/500px-Musella_lasiocarpa_at_Hampton_Court_Flower_Show.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Musella_lasiocarpa_at_Hampton_Court_Flower_Show.jpg/1280px-Musella_lasiocarpa_at_Hampton_Court_Flower_Show.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Musella_lasiocarpa_at_Hampton_Court_Flower_Show.jpg/500px-Musella_lasiocarpa_at_Hampton_Court_Flower_Show.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMusella_lasiocarpa_at_Hampton_Court_Flower_Show.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.j